


QUOTA(1)            UNIX Programmer's Manual             QUOTA(1)



NAME
     quota - display disk usage and limits

SYNOPSIS
     quota [ -v ] [ user ]

DESCRIPTION
     _Q_u_o_t_a displays users' disk usage and limits. Only the
     super-user may use the optional _u_s_e_r argument to view the
     limits of users other than himself.

     _Q_u_o_t_a without options displays only warnings about mounted
     file systems where usage is over quota.

OPTIONS
     -v   display user's quotas on all mounted file systems where
          quotas exist.

FILES
     _q_u_o_t_a_s              quota file at the file system root

SEE ALSO
     quotactl(2), quotaon(8), edquota(8), rquotad(8c)
































